---
title: German Civil Code (BGB §622 Notice Periods for Employment Contracts)
sourceType: statutory_statute
date: 2025-01-01
jurisdiction: Germany
language: en
register: statutory_legal
format: pdf
---

The statutory notice period for termination of an employment relationship is four weeks to the fifteenth day or to the end of a calendar month.

For termination by the employer, the notice period increases progressively according to the duration of employment: after two years of service, one month to the end of a calendar month; after five years of service, two months to the end of a calendar month; after eight years of service, three months to the end of a calendar month.

Any individual contractual agreement providing for a shorter notice period than the statutory minimum under §622 is invalid, unless expressly permitted by an authorized collective bargaining agreement.
